{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789855357,"nonce":"AYGb6QKMdiMf8gsOHCQk5WybxLs=","message":"Fixed in 1d8f09a. Cause: wren_super_call_N resolved the superclass from JitContext.defining_class, which is set when the interpreter enters compiled code but not by a direct JIT-to-JIT call, so Child.compute()'s super.compute(), entered directly from Container.result()'s compiled body, walked up from whatever class the context last named and found no method — hence the null, and the timing dependence on which bodies had been installed. Compiled super calls now pass the method's defining class (method_binding at compile time) through wren_super_call_from_N, which sets the context for the dispatch and restores it. 0/120 failures after (9/40 before) in tiered mode, Cranelift-only and with LLVM forced early.","files":null}]}